name c01m04-rivers-run-deep
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T07:20:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 4 OF 10 -- {Rivers Run Deep}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 14 goals -- 3 + 4 Werewolves, 2 T-80s and 5 Geckos -- and the briefing gives an
# ORDER: "the squadron of Werewolves giving air support ... we recommend that you take them out
# first."
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 2 (Canyonlands, Utah, terrain.md 6), night -- sun -65.11 deg at the lead's
# spawn, computed by the runner. 14 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 7 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 7 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 5 Gecko -> `sa8` - wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 8, Stinger 8, artillery 6, wingman 8, fuel
# 8000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 40` = 8000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all 14 goals. The briefing orders the Werewolves killed FIRST, so telemetry
#   must carry the kill ORDER or the tactical claim of this mission cannot be checked at all.
#   MEASURED: it cannot be checked. No Werewolf in this tree can be killed by anything (D2), so the
#   ordering claim has no object and this file measures the ground half only.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count. exit 1 on `two` = a damaged flight.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): FOUR OF FOURTEEN, and FIVE objects destroyed.
#   t = 20.7 / 24.0 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 11.23 and 2.54; t04+g04 and t06+t07+g05 die
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 4 of 14 met, `survive` met; `two` SUCCESS. 18 SA-8 launches,
#                       closest 18.28 m, no hit.
#   THE ORDERING CLAIM IS UNMEASURED and cannot be measured: 0 of the 7 Werewolves can be engaged.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m04 1
  spawn 38.17225 -109.89465 150 347.9 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 40
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 38.20375 -109.90322 150 300
  wp 38.23848 -109.91268 1000 300
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit g03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit g04
  objective kill unit t06
  objective kill unit g05
  objective kill unit w01
  objective kill unit w02
  objective kill unit w03
  objective kill unit w04
  objective kill unit w05
  objective kill unit w06
  objective kill unit w07
  objective survive

